Ladybird revokes a removed extension, then deletes its storage directory
on the storage worker, behind any pending writes. Disabling an extension
keeps its storage, and a failed deletion is logged.

Chromium deletes storage asynchronously too, with StorageFrontend::
DeleteStorageSoon(), which posts the deletion to ValueStoreCache::
DeleteStorageSoon() for each backend. Gecko clears both storage backends
on uninstall, in Extension.sys.mjs’s onUninstalled handler, through
ExtensionStorage.clear() and clearStoragesForPrincipal(). And WebKit’s
WebExtensionController::removeStorage() deletes the SQLite database and
reports any error to its completion handler, where Ladybird logs it.
